Here's TUnit's lifecycle at each scope:

## 1. Before/After Every Individual Test

```csharp
public class OrderTests
{
    [Before(Test)]
    public async Task ResetDatabase(TestContext context)
    {
        await InMemoryDb.ResetAsync();
    }

    [After(Test)]
    public async Task Cleanup(TestContext context)
    {
        // runs after each test
    }

    [Test]
    public async Task Order_WithNoItems_Throws() { /* ... */ }
}
```

You can also use **constructor** / `IDisposable.Dispose` / `IAsyncDisposable.DisposeAsync` for per-test setup/teardown.

## 2. Once Per Class (Class-Scoped Fixture)

```csharp
public class CustomerApiTests
{
    [Before(Class)]
    public static async Task OpenFixture(ClassHookContext context)
    {
        // runs once before the first test in this class
    }

    [After(Class)]
    public static async Task DisposeFixture(ClassHookContext context)
    {
        // runs once after the last test in this class
    }

    [Test]
    public async Task GetCustomer_ReturnsOk() { /* ... */ }
}
```

Note: class-level hooks must be **static**.

## 3. Once Per Assembly

```csharp
public class WireMockSetup
{
    [Before(Assembly)]
    public static async Task StartWireMock(AssemblyHookContext context)
    {
        // starts once before any test in this assembly
    }

    [After(Assembly)]
    public static async Task StopWireMock(AssemblyHookContext context)
    {
        // stops once after all tests in this assembly finish
    }
}
```

## 4. Once Per Entire Test Session

```csharp
public class GlobalDatabaseSetup
{
    [Before(TestSession)]
    public static async Task ApplyMigrations(TestSessionContext context)
    {
        // very first thing — e.g. run EF Core migrations
    }

    [After(TestSession)]
    public static async Task TearDownDatabase(TestSessionContext context)
    {
        // very last thing — drop the database
    }
}
```

---

### Quick Reference

| Scope | Before | After | Method must be |
|-------|--------|-------|----------------|
| Each test | `[Before(Test)]` | `[After(Test)]` | Instance |
| Class | `[Before(Class)]` | `[After(Class)]` | **Static** |
| Assembly | `[Before(Assembly)]` | `[After(Assembly)]` | **Static** |
| Session | `[Before(TestSession)]` | `[After(TestSession)]` | **Static** |

**Bonus — global cross-cutting hooks:** Use `[BeforeEvery(Test)]` / `[AfterEvery(Test)]` (also `Class`/`Assembly` variants) to run logic for *every* test/class across the entire run (e.g., logging, timing) from a single hook class. All hooks optionally accept a `CancellationToken` parameter.
